1
00:00:03,219 --> 00:00:06,880
Chapter 26.

2
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:15,039
Beside the well there was the ruin of an old Stone Wall

3
00:00:15,039 --> 00:00:20,439
When I came back from my work, the next evening, I saw from some distance away my little

4
00:00:20,439 --> 00:00:25,238
prince sitting on top of this wall, with his feet dangling.

5
00:00:25,238 --> 00:00:33,158
And I heard him say: "Then you don't remember. This is not the exact spot."

6
00:00:33,158 --> 00:00:38,198
Another voice must have answered him, for he replied to it:

7
00:00:38,198 --> 00:00:44,079
"Yes, yes! It is the right day, but this is not the place."

8
00:00:44,079 --> 00:00:50,500
I continued my walk toward the war At no time did I see or hear anyone.

9
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:57,520
The little prince, however, replied once again: "--Exactly. You will see where my track

10
00:00:57,520 --> 00:01:01,840
begins, in the sand. You have nothing to do but wait for me there.

11
00:01:01,840 --> 00:01:04,899
I shall be there tonight."

12
00:01:04,899 --> 00:01:09,520
I was only 20 yards from the wall, and I still saw nothing.

13
00:01:09,520 --> 00:01:16,840
After a silence the little prince spoke again: "You have good poison?

14
00:01:16,840 --> 00:01:22,260
You are sure that it will not make me suffer too long?"

15
00:01:22,599 --> 00:01:30,279
I stopped in my tracks, my heart torn asunder; but still I did not understand.

16
00:01:30,279 --> 00:01:33,880
"Now go away," said the little prince.

17
00:01:33,880 --> 00:01:37,359
"I want to get down from the wall."

18
00:01:37,359 --> 00:01:42,460
I dropped my eyes, then, to the foot of the wall-- and I leaped into the air.

19
00:01:42,460 --> 00:01:47,139
There before me, facing the little prince, was one of those yellow snakes that take

20
00:01:47,139 --> 00:01:50,260
30 seconds to bring your life to an end.

21
00:01:50,260 --> 00:01:54,039
Even as I was digging into my pocket to get out my revolver I made a running

22
00:01:54,039 --> 00:01:55,359
step back.

23
00:01:55,359 --> 00:02:00,399
But the noise I made, the snake let himself flow easily across the sand like

24
00:02:00,399 --> 00:02:07,420
the dying spray of a fountain, and, in no apparent hurry, disappeared,

25
00:02:07,420 --> 00:02:13,679
with a light metallic sound, among the stones.

26
00:02:14,079 --> 00:02:18,939
I reached the wall just in time to catch my little man in my arms; his face was

27
00:02:18,939 --> 00:02:21,899
white as snow.

28
00:02:22,118 --> 00:02:24,158
"What does this mean?"

29
00:02:24,158 --> 00:02:26,039
I demanded.

30
00:02:26,039 --> 00:02:29,800
"Why are you talking with snakes?"

31
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:34,479
I had loosened the golden muffler that he always wore I'd moistened his temples,

32
00:02:34,479 --> 00:02:37,658
and had given him some more water to drink.

33
00:02:37,658 --> 00:02:42,359
And now I did not dare ask him any more questions.

34
00:02:42,399 --> 00:02:47,560
He looked at me very gravely, and put his arms around my neck.

35
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:55,840
I felt his heart beating like the heart of a dying bird, shot with someone's rifle...

36
00:02:55,840 --> 00:03:03,158
"I am glad that you have found what was the matter with your engine," he said.

37
00:03:03,158 --> 00:03:09,399
"Now you can go back home--" "How do you know about that?"

38
00:03:09,399 --> 00:03:13,000
I was just coming to tell him that my work had been successful, beyond anything

39
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:15,760
that I had dared to hope.

40
00:03:15,760 --> 00:03:25,000
He made no answer to my question, but he added: "I, too, am going back home today..."

41
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:32,560
Then, sadly-- "It is much farther...

42
00:03:32,560 --> 00:03:38,760
it is much more difficult..."

43
00:03:38,979 --> 00:03:44,020
I realize clearly that something extraordinary was happening.

44
00:03:44,020 --> 00:03:47,800
I was holding him close in my arms as if he were a little child;

45
00:03:47,800 --> 00:03:51,520
and yet it seemed to me that he was rushing headlong toward an abyss from

46
00:03:51,520 --> 00:03:55,238
which I could do nothing to restrain him...

47
00:03:55,238 --> 00:04:02,819
His luck was very serious, like someone lost far away.

48
00:04:03,460 --> 00:04:07,118
"I have your sheep.

49
00:04:07,118 --> 00:04:11,139
And I have the sheep's box.

50
00:04:11,139 --> 00:04:18,359
And I have the muscle And he gave me a sad smile.

51
00:04:18,578 --> 00:04:21,219
I waited a long time.

52
00:04:21,219 --> 00:04:25,920
I could see that he was reviving little by little.

53
00:04:26,020 --> 00:04:33,578
"Dear little man," I said to him, "you are afraid..."

54
00:04:33,578 --> 00:04:38,500
He was afraid, there was no doubt about that.

55
00:04:38,500 --> 00:04:42,118
But he laughed lightly.

56
00:04:43,420 --> 00:04:48,219
"I am going to be much more afraid this evening..."

57
00:04:48,219 --> 00:04:54,039
Once again I felt myself frozen by the sense of something irrepairable And I

58
00:04:54,039 --> 00:04:58,599
knew that I could not bear the thought of never hearing that laughter anymore

59
00:04:58,599 --> 00:05:04,420
For me, it was like a spring of fresh water in the desert.

60
00:05:04,420 --> 00:05:11,439
"Little man," I said, "I want to hear you laugh again."

61
00:05:11,439 --> 00:05:17,020
But he said to me: "Tonight, it will be a year...

62
00:05:17,020 --> 00:05:21,760
my star, then, can be found right above the place where I came to the Earth, a

63
00:05:21,760 --> 00:05:24,039
year ago..."

64
00:05:24,039 --> 00:05:30,039
"Little man," I said, "tell me that it is only a bad dream--

65
00:05:30,039 --> 00:05:35,139
this affair of the snake, and the meeting place and the star..."

66
00:05:35,139 --> 00:05:38,078
But he did not answer my plea.

67
00:05:38,078 --> 00:05:45,960
He said to me, instead: "The thing that is important is the thing that is not seen..."

68
00:05:45,960 --> 00:05:48,760
"Yes, I know..."

69
00:05:48,760 --> 00:05:51,520
"It is just as it is with the flower. If

70
00:05:51,520 --> 00:05:53,139
you love a flower that lives on a star,

71
00:05:53,139 --> 00:05:56,319
it is sweet to look at the sky at night.

72
00:05:56,319 --> 00:05:59,738
All the stars are a bloom with flowers..."

73
00:05:59,738 --> 00:06:02,198
"Yes, I know..."

74
00:06:02,198 --> 00:06:05,139
"It is just as it is with the water.

75
00:06:05,139 --> 00:06:10,539
Because of the pulley, and the rope, what you gave me to drink was like music.

76
00:06:10,539 --> 00:06:14,500
You remember-- how good it was."

77
00:06:14,500 --> 00:06:18,218
"Yes, I know..."

78
00:06:18,218 --> 00:06:22,239
"And at night you will look up at the stars.

79
00:06:22,239 --> 00:06:26,920
Where I live everything is so small that I cannot show you where my star is to be

80
00:06:26,920 --> 00:06:28,120
found.

81
00:06:28,120 --> 00:06:30,398
It is better, like that.

82
00:06:30,398 --> 00:06:34,179
My star will be just one of the stars, for you.

83
00:06:34,179 --> 00:06:38,978
And so you will love to watch all the stars in the heavens...

84
00:06:38,978 --> 00:06:42,099
they will all be your friends.

85
00:06:42,099 --> 00:06:48,218
And, besides I'm going to make you a present..."

86
00:06:48,218 --> 00:06:50,739
He laughed again.

87
00:06:50,739 --> 00:06:59,500
"Ah, little prince, dear little prince I'd love to hear that laughter!"

88
00:06:59,500 --> 00:07:01,780
"That is my present.

89
00:07:01,780 --> 00:07:03,638
Just that.

90
00:07:03,638 --> 00:07:07,978
It will be as it was when we drank the water..."

91
00:07:08,700 --> 00:07:12,398
"What are you trying to say?"

92
00:07:12,398 --> 00:07:20,079
"All men have stars," he answered, "but they are not the same things for different people.

93
00:07:20,079 --> 00:07:26,739
For some, who are Travelers the stars are guides. For others they are no more than

94
00:07:26,739 --> 00:07:28,898
little lights in the sky.

95
00:07:28,898 --> 00:07:32,439
For others, who are scholars, they are problems.

96
00:07:32,439 --> 00:07:35,500
For my businessmen they are wealth.

97
00:07:35,500 --> 00:07:39,819
But all these stars are silent.

98
00:07:39,819 --> 00:07:47,638
You-- you alone-- will have the stars as no one else has them--"

99
00:07:48,579 --> 00:07:52,000
"What are you trying to say?"

100
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:55,898
"In one of the stars I shall be living.

101
00:07:55,898 --> 00:07:59,079
In one of them I shall be laughing. And

102
00:07:59,079 --> 00:08:03,280
so it will be as if all the stars were laughing, when you look at the sky at

103
00:08:03,280 --> 00:08:04,478
night...

104
00:08:04,478 --> 00:08:12,340
you-- only you-- will have stars that can laugh!"

105
00:08:12,340 --> 00:08:14,978
And he laughed again.

106
00:08:14,978 --> 00:08:20,079
"And when your sorrow is comforted (time soothes all sorrows

107
00:08:20,079 --> 00:08:23,079
you'll be content that you have known me.

108
00:08:23,079 --> 00:08:28,840
You will always be my friend. You will want to laugh with me. And you will

109
00:08:28,840 --> 00:08:32,260
sometimes open your window, so, for that pleasure...

110
00:08:32,260 --> 00:08:35,920
and your friends will be properly astonished to see you laughing as you

111
00:08:35,920 --> 00:08:42,398
look up the sky! Then you will say to them, 'Yes, the stars always make me laugh!'

112
00:08:42,398 --> 00:08:45,040
And they will think you are crazy.

113
00:08:45,040 --> 00:08:49,540
It will be a very shabby trick that I shall have played on you..."

114
00:08:49,540 --> 00:08:52,359
And he laughed again.

115
00:08:52,359 --> 00:08:55,718
"It will be as if, in place of the stars, I

116
00:08:55,718 --> 00:09:00,939
had given you a great number of little bells that knew how to laugh..."

117
00:09:00,939 --> 00:09:04,439
And he laughed again.

118
00:09:04,599 --> 00:09:12,398
Then he quickly became serious: "Tonight-- you know...

119
00:09:12,398 --> 00:09:19,239
do not come I shall not leave you," I said.

120
00:09:19,239 --> 00:09:21,879
"I shall look as if I was suffering.

121
00:09:21,879 --> 00:09:25,840
I shall look a little as if I were dying.

122
00:09:25,840 --> 00:09:27,939
It is like that.

123
00:09:27,939 --> 00:09:30,159
Do not come to see that.

124
00:09:30,159 --> 00:09:33,040
It is not worth the trouble..."

125
00:09:33,040 --> 00:09:37,059
"I shall not leave you."

126
00:09:37,059 --> 00:09:39,700
But he was worried.

127
00:09:39,700 --> 00:09:44,500
"I tell you-- it is also because of the snake.

128
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:46,478
He must not bite you.

129
00:09:46,478 --> 00:09:51,100
Snakes-- they are very malicious creatures.

130
00:09:51,100 --> 00:09:55,299
This one might bite you just for fun..."

131
00:09:55,299 --> 00:10:00,159
"I shall not leave you."

132
00:10:00,159 --> 00:10:04,739
But a thought came to reassure him:

133
00:10:05,200 --> 00:10:11,459
"It is true that they have no more poison for a second bite."

134
00:10:13,540 --> 00:10:17,680
That night I did not see him set out on his way.

135
00:10:17,680 --> 00:10:21,700
He got away from me without making a sound.

136
00:10:21,700 --> 00:10:27,459
When I succeeded in catching up with him he was walking along with a quick and resolute step.

137
00:10:27,459 --> 00:10:31,600
He said to me merely: "Ah!

138
00:10:31,600 --> 00:10:33,879
You are there..."

139
00:10:33,879 --> 00:10:36,459
And he took me by the hand.

140
00:10:36,459 --> 00:10:39,639
But he was still worrying.

141
00:10:39,639 --> 00:10:43,239
"It was wrong of you to come. You will suffer.

142
00:10:43,239 --> 00:10:49,000
I shall look as if I were dead; and and that would not be true..."

143
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:51,700
I said nothing.

144
00:10:51,700 --> 00:10:54,159
"You understand...

145
00:10:54,159 --> 00:10:56,559
it is too far.

146
00:10:56,559 --> 00:10:59,978
I cannot carry this body with me.

147
00:10:59,978 --> 00:11:03,398
It is too heavy."

148
00:11:03,398 --> 00:11:06,398
I said nothing.

149
00:11:06,398 --> 00:11:13,600
"But it will be like an old abandoned shell. There is nothing sad about old shells..."

150
00:11:13,600 --> 00:11:16,859
I said nothing.

151
00:11:16,898 --> 00:11:19,359
He was a little discouraged.

152
00:11:19,359 --> 00:11:25,478
But he made one more effort: "You know, it would be very nice.

153
00:11:25,478 --> 00:11:28,359
I, too, shall look at the stars.

154
00:11:28,359 --> 00:11:33,760
All the stars will be wells with a rusty pulley. All the stars will pour out fresh

155
00:11:33,760 --> 00:11:37,020
water for me to drink..."

156
00:11:37,420 --> 00:11:40,559
I said nothing

157
00:11:40,959 --> 00:11:43,239
it will be so amusing!

158
00:11:43,239 --> 00:11:52,859
You will have 500 million little bells, and I shall have 500 million springs of fresh water..."

159
00:11:53,500 --> 00:11:57,659
And he too said nothing more,

160
00:11:57,939 --> 00:12:01,500
because he was crying...

161
00:12:02,559 --> 00:12:05,020
"Here it is.

162
00:12:05,020 --> 00:12:08,579
Let me go on by myself."

163
00:12:08,739 --> 00:12:13,420
And he sat down, because he was afraid.

164
00:12:13,420 --> 00:12:16,680
Then he said, again:

165
00:12:17,079 --> 00:12:21,659
"You know-- my flower...

166
00:12:21,700 --> 00:12:24,760
I am responsible for her.

167
00:12:24,760 --> 00:12:32,200
And she is so weak she's so naive She has four thorns, of no use at all, to

168
00:12:32,200 --> 00:12:36,478
protect herself against all the world..."

169
00:12:37,719 --> 00:12:45,540
I too sat down, because I was not able to stand up any longer.

170
00:12:47,680 --> 00:12:53,579
"There now-- that is all..."

171
00:12:53,799 --> 00:12:59,760
He still hesitated a little; then he got up.

172
00:12:59,799 --> 00:13:03,159
He took one step.

173
00:13:03,159 --> 00:13:06,478
I could not move.

174
00:13:08,799 --> 00:13:13,540
There was nothing there but a flash of yellow closed his ankle.

175
00:13:13,540 --> 00:13:17,260
He remained motionless for an instant.

176
00:13:17,260 --> 00:13:20,318
He did not cry out.

177
00:13:20,318 --> 00:13:25,020
He fell as gently as a tree falls.

178
00:13:25,359 --> 00:13:31,978
There was not even any sound, because of the sand
